    "title": "CHP searches for SUV that struck, killed man on I-5 off-ramp near Bankers Hill - NewsBreak",
    "text": "(FOX 5/KUSI) San Diego — The California Highway Patrol is asking for the public’s help in locating the driver of a vehicle that was allegedly involved in a fatal hit-and-run incident in mid-June. The agency said the crash happened on the Hawthorn Street offramp of I-5 north on June 20 at around 12:44 a.m. The CHP said a dark SUV with noticeable front-end damage was on the off-ramp when it struck a man and fled from the scene. The man who was hit succumbed to his injuries and died. The victim’s name is being withheld until his family is notified. The CHP said officers are searching for a dark colored SUV and that a toxicology report is pending to determine if drugs or alcohol were a factor. Anyone who witnessed the crash or has any information regarding the suspect or vehicle is encouraged to contact the San Diego CHP at (858) 293-6000. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX 5 San Diego & KUSI News.",
